# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Product copy of the format settings of the Crux template sources: LLVM with Linux brace
# placement, 4-space indent, 100 columns. The sources of this template conform to it, and a test
# compares its settings with Crux's own .clang-format, so the two cannot drift apart unnoticed.
#
# Copy this file to the root of the product repository. Zephyr itself formats with tabs. A driver
# that is meant for upstream Zephyr should use Zephyr's own .clang-format instead: put it in that
# driver's directory, where clang-format finds it first.
# That holds only once the copy is at the product root: without it, check-format.sh passes this
# file with --style=file:, which applies to every file and overrides a nested .clang-format.
# See docs/coding-guidelines.md in Crux.
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
BreakBeforeBraces: Linux
IndentWidth: 4
ColumnLimit: 100
SortIncludes: CaseSensitive
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: None
AllowShortBlocksOnASingleLine: Never
IndentExternBlock: NoIndent
